<title>SOUTH KOREA: Korea Heavy signs $223 mln India power plant deal.</title>
<headline>Korea Heavy signs $223 mln India power plant deal.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's state-run Korea Heavy Industries and Construction Co said on Thursday it had signed a $223 million contract with India's Essar Power Ltd to build a thermoelectric power plant in India on a turn-key basis.  </p>
<p>A statement from Korea Heavy said the plant, with a capacity of 330 megawatts, would be constructed within the Madya Pradesh state by March 2000.</p>
<p>It said the plant would have two gas turbines, two heat recovery steam generators and a steam turbine.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
